# Improved SMPL (0.2.0-experimental, then named Fine Tune + Sample Rate): in GRID RECORDING a held trig's TUN lock takes
# cents too: trig on step 1 of BD, held; the first nudge only shows the value (the held trig's
# knob swallows it, emulator), the second, +4, reads +0.05 on the inverted, locked knob (one
# step of acceleration, as in sample-rate-fine-tun).
# Places a trig on BD step 1 of the active pattern and takes it off again; leaves GRID RECORDING.
# Run stopped. BD's TUN at +0 (CC 24 64). Needs BD step 1 of the active pattern empty (a trig there
# would be taken off and put back without its locks). If the run stops inside this case, GRID
# RECORDING is on and a trig sits on BD step 1: press RECORD, then T1.
# SMPL is pressed from AMP, never on its own page (that toggles the knob and waveform views), so
# the SAMPLE page keeps the view it had: the unit references are its waveform view.
name: sample-rate-fine-lock
state: changes

hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key AMP
wait 300
key SMPL
wait 3500
cc 24 64
key RECORD
wait 300
key T1
wait 300
hold T1
wait 300
nudge A +4
wait 750
screen lockA
nudge A +4
wait 750
screen lockB
expect lockB == ref region 0 9 34 9
release T1
wait 300
key T1
wait 300
key RECORD
